      "message": "It's fixed. `slugify` no longer produces repeated dashes.\n\nThe bug was in `slug/core.py`: every non-alphanumeric character became its own `-`, so `\"Hello, World!\"` came out as `hello--world-`. The fix only adds a dash when the last character wasn't already one, and strips leading and trailing dashes.\n\nA quick manual check gave the expected output for these inputs:\n- `Hello World` → `hello-world`\n- `Hello, World!` → `hello-world`\n- `a  --  b` → `a-b`\n- `!!hi!!` → `hi`\n\nI didn't run the test suite, as you asked. The existing tests cover `Hello World` and `ABC`, and both still produce the same output.\n\nOne thing I changed beyond the literal bug: I also strip leading and trailing dashes. If you'd rather keep those, it's a one-line revert.",
